    "configName": "Clairnote SN (reproduction study)",
    "fileSuffix": "-ClairnoteSN",
    "notationLabel": "Clairnote SN — reproduction study",
    "notationFootnote": "",
    "author": "Paul Morris",
    "description": "Reproduction study — inspired by Clairnote SN (Paul Morris, 2018). Major-third 2-line staff at E/G#; the internal floating ledgers for D/F#/A# plus the C ledger are override templates (per the operator reference). The C ledger shows for C/C#/D; the operator's rule also lists A#/B, but those sit below the C-boundary where the platform's C-aligned ledger regions would place the ledger at the wrong (lower) C across an intervening staff line, so they are trimmed and the limitation is documented as a gap. Uniform duration-carrying ovals. Clairnote's own key signatures (session 55): a dot for each note of the key in stacks that change at each change of odd and even, a tail up on each flat and down on each sharp, the tails imported as filled shapes. Clairnote's alternative CLEF form is not shown in the sources, so no clef is authored (omission); its alternative accidental signs need the unimplemented accidental enhancement (E4) — documented deviation. Design CC BY-SA 4.0; no code ported from clairnote.ly. Built from the public gallery description/image; not endorsed by or derived from the original.",
    "systemName": "Clairnote SN",
    "systemCreator": "Paul Morris",
    "systemYear": 2018,
    "sourceUrl": "https://musicnotation.org/system/clairnote-sn-paul-morris/",
    "reproductionStudy": true,
    "created": null,
    "modified": null
  }
